CHAPTER VI
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 29 (1) The Regent may appoint officials or relevant Regional Apparatus to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of Women and Children Protection.
(2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. provision of implementation instructions;
b. guidance;
c. supervision;
d. monitoring; and
e. evaluation of the Implementation of Women and Children Protection.

